---
description: OpenChamber is a Droplet for Droppy, built with DroppyKit. The brief, the build loop and the rules live in AGENTS.md at the package root.
alwaysApply: true
---

Read `AGENTS.md` at the package root before changing anything in this package. It carries the loop (`droppykit build`, `droppykit validate`, `droppykit run -- --shots ./shots --report ./shots/report.json`), the rules a droplet must follow, and the on-disk paths of the DroppyKit guides and sources under `/Users/josuegalre/projects/personal/droppykit`.

Before `droppykit submit`, work through AGENTS.md's "Before `droppykit submit`" list: the scaffold's avatar, summary, changelog and README are placeholders the Store refuses. Follow its icon, settings pane and good citizen sections too.

Never build the bundle with a bare `swift build`; only `droppykit build` produces one Droppy can load. Never make, draw or replace the droplet's icon: Jordy designs every Store droplet's icon, and `Openchamber.icon` is a placeholder for the harness that `droppykit submit` leaves out. Keep `droplet.json` `surfaces` and the droplet's protocol conformances in agreement. After every visual change render the shots and look at them: the DroppyKit MCP server in `.cursor/mcp.json` returns them inline through `droppykit_shots`, and `droppykit_install` puts the bundle into Droppy Playground and reports whether it loaded.

Shelf widgets: pad once with `context.contentInsets`; alone on a notched Mac or the camera island, wrap the header row around the camera through `ShelfWidgetNotchWrapTraits` and `context.notchWrap`, drawn with `ShelfWidgetNotchWrapRow`, and never offset it yourself; the compact row is the shell's own height on every display (a 32pt Air notch, the 31pt camera pill, the island with the user's offset), so size to `DroppyLiveActivityMetrics.rowHeight(on:)` and branch on `notchGeometry.compactShell`; every control is the wash, `DroppyWashCircleButtonStyle` or `DroppyWashPillButtonStyle` at `context.washControlSize` (34pt alone, 28pt paired or beside the camera, 24pt in a list row, `.neutral` except the one action the widget is for), a switch is `DroppyWashChoiceButtonStyle`, never glass or a segmented picker; no clicks mid-spring (`.allowsHitTesting(!context.isShelfTransitioning)`). The droplet's icon follows the user's icon style with no code.
